# The E2E harness and its runtime artifacts never belong in the application
# image: it is a separate, throwaway test container, not something the
# Dockerfile builds or ships (docs/specs/05-frontend-pwa-foundations.md).
# node_modules in particular has broken this build before — npm's symlinks,
# written through the e2e/ bind mount, are not something Docker's tar-based
# build context reader tolerates.
e2e/
